      "stage": 3,
      "version": "9.0.1",
      "nevra": null,
      "note": "negativo17 builds Fedora's ffmpeg source with every codec on and no package suffix, so its command-line tool is `ffmpeg`. The same source built the way Fedora builds it sets `%global pkg_suffix -free` and names the tool `ffmpeg-free`. Same recipe, same binaries, different name; the free flavour carries no `Provides: ffmpeg`, so a transaction asking for the literal name still needs this mapping read."
    },
    {
      "requirement": "ffmpeg-libs",
      "origin": "codec-transaction",
      "status": "equivalent",
      "factory_source": "ffmpeg",
      "factory_binary": "libavcodec-free",
      "upstream_spec_source": "https://github.com/rpmfusion/ffmpeg",
      "recipe": "packages/ffmpeg",
      "stage": 3,
      "version": "9.0.1",
      "nevra": null,
      "note": "`ffmpeg-libs` is negativo17's single bundle of the FFmpeg shared libraries. Fedora splits the same libraries into libavcodec-free, libavdevice-free, libavfilter-free, libavformat-free, libavutil-free, libswresample-free and libswscale-free, every one of them from `packages/ffmpeg`. Nothing links `ffmpeg-libs` by name -- consumers link the sonames -- so the split satisfies it. The binary recorded here is libavcodec-free because it is the member every other one requires."
    },
